        {
          "id": 2214278359,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Well, preferably the functions in `wsutil/filesystem` would do something consistent and sensible if called when it hasn't been initialized. Right now the various functions sometimes return the Wireshark directories, sometimes the Stratoshark directories, and sometimes the current working directory if called when uninitialized.\n\nDumpcap links with libustil, so sometimes the functions get called. They probably shouldn't.",
